`RecordRepository` stores records by ID in first-insertion order. IDs must be nonblank after trimming, otherwise `RangeError` is thrown. `save` copies its input; saving an existing ID replaces the value without changing order. `find` returns a fresh record or null. `all` returns fresh records in insertion order. `remove` returns whether a record existed. Returned records must never alias stored records, and caller mutation after `save` must not affect storage.

Known-bad source:

```ts
export interface DataRecord {
  id: string;
  label: string;
}

export class RecordRepository {
  private readonly records = new Map<string, DataRecord>();

  save(record: DataRecord): void {
    if (record.id.trim().length === 0) throw new RangeError("id must not be blank");
    this.records.set(record.id, { id: record.id, label: record.label });
  }

  find(id: string): DataRecord | null {
    return this.records.get(id) ?? null;
  }

  all(): DataRecord[] {
    return Array.from(this.records.values(), (record) => ({ ...record }));
  }

  remove(id: string): boolean {
    return this.records.delete(id);
  }
}
```

